  "narration": {
    "title": "Milwaukee's Best Record, but the Dodgers Hold Top",
    "intro": "Nobody in baseball has a better record than the Brewers at 93-57, yet the Dodgers still sit first. Two clubs made big leaps this week: San Diego went perfect, and Detroit climbed into the top ten. Here's where everyone stands.",
    "power_lead": "The Dodgers hold the top spot at 90-59 despite Milwaukee's superior 93-57 record, with Teoscar Hern\u00e1ndez (7-for-16, 1.276 OPS) and Mookie Betts leading a 4-2 week. Milwaukee sits second on a 5-1, plus-27 week powered by Brice Turang's 10-for-19 and two homers. The loudest movers were San Diego, up eleven to sixth on a 6-0 sweep behind Jackson Merrill's 12-for-25 and 12 RBI, and Detroit, up thirteen to tenth on a 5-1 run with Riley Greene driving in nine. Atlanta paid for a 3-4 week, sliding six spots to seventh."
  }
